\section{Comparing multiple q values}{
To statistically compare Tsallis entropy across multiple q values between groups, use the \code{compare_q_values} function:
\itemize{
  \item For unpaired groups: Wilcoxon test is performed for each q value.
  \item For paired/repeated measures: Friedman test is performed across q values within each group (requires subject IDs).
}
This enables robust analysis of how the choice of q affects group differences in splicing diversity.
}
\section{Statistical analysis}{
For comparing Tsallis entropy values between groups or conditions, the following statistical tests are recommended:
\itemize{
  \item Wilcoxon rank sum test: For two unpaired groups.
  \item Wilcoxon signed-rank test: For two paired groups.
  \item Permutation test: For robust, non-parametric assessment, especially with small sample sizes.
}
These tests are implemented in the package and can be selected via the \code{test} argument in \code{calculate_difference}.
}

